SUMMARY:Boston Day Trip to the MFABoston
DTSTART;TZID=America/New_York:20260731T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20260731T170000
DTSTAMP:20260725T193708Z
UID:dartmouth-groups-1630964@free-food-dartmouth
SEQUENCE:0
CLASS:PUBLIC
DESCRIPTION:Original event page(s):\nhttps://dartmouthgroups.dartmouth.edu
 /rsvp_boot?id=1630964\nhttps://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSdMpelH0LK
 2PeKSZGpmN52DcMVaHv1vqCVZHGw3lklw2ANuSw/viewform?usp=send_form\n\nDescript
 ion:\nRSVP is required. Event is open to all Dartmouth undergraduate\, gra
 duate and professional students\nTake a break from campus and join us for 
 a trip to the Museum of Fine Arts\, Boston! Discover everything from iconi
 c paintings and ancient artifacts to contemporary installations and intera
 ctive exhibits. Whether you're an art lover\, looking for inspiration\, or
  just want to explore one of Boston's most famous cultural destinations wi
 th friends\, there's something for everyone. Come experience world-class a
 rt\, connect with fellow students\, and enjoy a fun day in the city!\nThe 
 Office of Pluralism & Leadership will be providing transportation to and f
 rom Boston and snacks and lunch are included\, so all you have to do is sh
 ow up and enjoy the experience. Come explore world-class art\, connect wit
 h fellow students\, and spend a fun day in the city!\nRSVP is required. Ev
 ent is open to all Dartmouth undergraduate\, graduate and professional stu
 dents.\nRegistration will close July 29th unless all spots are claimed bef
 ore then.\nWe look forward to seeing you there.\n______________________\nD
 etails at a quick glance:\nDate: Friday\, July 31\, 2026\nDeparture from c
 ampus at 8:00 AM in front of Rauner Library\nExplore MFA Boston 11:00 AM -
  1:00 PM\nLunch at Longwood Galleria 1:00 PM - 2:30 PM\nTravel back to cam
 pus 2:30 PM\n\nSponsor / organizer: Office of Pluralism and Leadership\n\n
 Source: Dartmouth Groups\n\nWhy this was included: explicit food-service w
 ording\; food keyword near service context\n\nFood availability is inferre
 d from the source listing\; verify details before attending.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260725T193708Z
LOCATION:Private Location (sign in to display)
STATUS:CONFIRMED
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dartmouthgroups.dartmouth.edu/rsvp_boot?id=1630964
X-MICROSOFT-CDO-BUSYSTATUS:FREE
